  "blocker": "DATA401 bulk decryption still blocked, but call graph now FULLY reversed (docs/DECRYPT-CALLGRAPH-2026-10-15.md, committed 60e0653 on branch watchdog/tekken6-decrypt-callgraph-20261015). PROVEN via full-ISO CRC scan: only sector 230256 of 417,807 has a valid CRC header \u2014 the per-sector CRC-key scheme covers just the header sector (first raw-LBN data sector, in an ISO fs gap right after the IDX at LBA 230240). The 0x8AA2CA8 stream cipher is called ONLY from 0x8AA305C (dual-decrypt+verify, CRC-sectors only) and the PRNG session-key path \u2014 the BULK does not use this cipher in any path found. IDX undecryptable with all candidate keys (ext, swapped, table@0x8B2B9F8, 0xBCBD1C51/0xE8BDE039). PPSSPP live-dump re-confirmed blocked (static-pie binary). Next: trace ktRead (0x08a9cdd0) vtable path for the bulk mechanism, or unicorn-emulate PAC open on IDX sectors.",
  "progress": "30% -> ~60%. Delay-slot CORRECTION (this run): 0x8AA1204 path Y K1=ext0 (old 'K1=buffer address' was a delay-slot misread) \u2014 dual-decrypt+verify empirically VALIDATED (0/506 mismatches vs 508/506 with old reading). ktRead chain traced: plain I/O, no crypto. 0x8AA135C proven DEAD (0 callers/refs). 0x8AA22E8 = save-data path (ms0:/PSP/SAVEDATA/%sDATA). IDX tail (sector 230252, bytes 1536-2047) is ZERO in clear => IDX not stream-encrypted. Bulk data region uniformly random, mechanism still unknown. Committed docs/DECRYPT-CORRECTIONS-2026-10-15.md as b7dd1aa (pushed).",
